  {
   "unit": "programs/obj/*/timefn.o",
   "failure": "playTests.sh dies with a segmentation fault as soon as the CLI takes a timestamp",
   "cause": "an aggregate of sixteen bytes or fewer is passed and returned indirectly, through a hidden pointer in x0, where AAPCS64 passes and returns it in general registers. A GCC caller therefore hands the callee the struct's value where the callee expects the address to write through.",
   "repro": "typedef struct { unsigned long long t; } T;\nT get(void) { T r; r.t = 42; return r; }\nunsigned long long span(T a, T b) { return b.t - a.t; }\n",
   "shownBy": "compile the three lines with EvoCC, call get() and span() from a GCC-compiled main, link and run: it faults where the GCC-compiled unit prints 42"
  }
 ],
